THE TABLE IS A GATE, NOT A CHORE
---------------------------------

`src/lib/licenses.ts` declares every bundled work with its version, its
licence, its upstream URL, and why it is bundled. Three checks keep it
complete, and all three fail rather than warn:

  * Every name in package.json's `dependencies` must have an entry, and every
    entry marked as a direct dependency must still be a declared one. Adding a
    dependency without adding it here fails `npm run assets:check`, which
    `npm run build` runs before it compiles anything.
  * Every font pinned in `models.lock.json` must have an entry whose licence
    string matches the lock. The font licences are copied from the lock, which
    is the manifest that already pins each file's size and sha256 — they are
    never retyped, because a licence string typed by hand is a licence string
    that is eventually wrong, and a wrong licence string is worse than none.
  * Every entry must appear in `public/licenses.html`, so the page a user reads
    cannot lag the table the build trusts.

`npm run test:coverage` is not the gate for any of this; the unit suite in
`src/components/ui/licenses.test.ts` and `scripts/verify-assets.mjs` are.

